  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 129 AM EDT Tue Aug 25 2026\n\nSurface high pressure leading to dry and comfortable conditions, \nwill continue today. Aloft, a closed upper low over Quebec is in the \nprocess of cycling away. The persistent SW ridge will hold on \nthrough much of the week. Troughing lifts north next weekend, \nallowing higher heights to move in the last days of August. Valley \nhighs in the lower 90s as well as increasing humidity will return \nas a result. \n\nPrecip chances will begin re-entering the forecast later tomorrow, \nwith the best probability over the Southern Appalachians. High \npressure moving to our east will allow southwesterly return flow to \ndevelop. Better coverage for showers and storms will come Thursday, \nas a weak cold front approaches from the northwest, as well as a \nwest to east draped stationary front to our south. Models show at \nleast 20kt bulk shear as well as CAPE near and above 1000 J/Kg \nThursday afternoon, so will need to monitor trends to see if strong \nto severe is possible.\n\nFollowing the frontal passage, surface high pressure fills in from \nthe north trying to dry out areas underneath it. The NBM, however, \ndoes keep some precipitation chances around over the weekend, but \nmainly for the mountains.",
